@echo off
rem Machine-local environment for run.cmd. Copy to env.cmd and edit.
rem
rem   copy env.cmd.example env.cmd
rem
rem env.cmd is in .gitignore: it describes this machine, not the program, and a
rem station's paths have no business in a commit. run.cmd calls it before
rem starting, so whatever is set here applies to every way the program is
rem started on this machine — one description of the machine, not two that drift
rem apart. This is the Windows counterpart of env.sh.example.

rem --- Interpreter ------------------------------------------------------------
rem Which python runs the program. Leave unset and run.cmd looks for a venv
rem beside the checkout, then falls back to python.exe from PATH.
rem set "PYTHON=C:\Python311\python.exe"
rem set "PYTHON=%~dp0venv\Scripts\python.exe"

rem If the dependencies live in a conda environment, activate it here instead of
rem setting PYTHON — the activation puts the right interpreter on PATH.
rem call C:\ProgramData\miniconda3\Scripts\activate.bat every-camera

rem --- DCAM-API (Japan camera) ------------------------------------------------
rem The Hamamatsu driver loads dcamapi.dll through ctypes (the vendored wrappers
rem in cameras\japan\dcamsdk\). The SDK's installer puts it in System32, which is
rem on the default DLL search path, so a station with the SDK installed normally
rem needs nothing here.
rem
rem Set this when the library lives elsewhere — an SDK unpacked rather than
rem installed, or two versions side by side. It names the file, and the error
rem message on a failed load lists every path that was tried, so a wrong value
rem says so immediately instead of at the start of a night.
rem set "DCAM_LIB=C:\Program Files\Hamamatsu\DCAM-API\dcamapi.dll"

rem --- Filter wheel -----------------------------------------------------------
rem Nothing to set: the COM port is a config.json setting (japan.filter_wheel.
rem port / asi.filter_wheel.port), not an environment variable. Find the number
rem in Device Manager under "Ports (COM & LPT)".

rem --- Earth rotation data (both sun-driven cameras) --------------------------
rem Solar altitude comes from astropy, which wants a fresh IERS table and by
rem default goes to datacenter.iers.org and maia.usno.navy.mil for it. Those two
rem hosts are routinely unreachable from a station that is otherwise online, so
rem the program does not ask for them: it uses the table astropy ships with, and
rem says so once per run. The missing UT1-UTC correction is worth about 0.004 deg
rem of solar altitude, against thresholds written in whole degrees.
rem
rem Set this only on a station that can reach those hosts and wants the fresher
rem table. It re-enables the download — including the wait on the first solar
rem calculation of each run if the host is slow — but it does NOT re-enable
rem astropy's exception: a stale table still returns a number rather than ending
rem the night. See the "Высота Солнца и данные о вращении Земли" section of
rem README.md.
rem set "EVERY_CAMERA_IERS_AUTO=1"

rem --- Anything else ----------------------------------------------------------
rem set "EVERY_CAMERA_SOMETHING=..."
